## Canonical Object Applicability

The 22 AOF canonical machine-readable object families are mapped in `.aof/applicability.yaml`. This mapping expresses project applicability; it does **not** claim that every required object has already been implemented in application code.

## Control Status and Gaps

- `.aof/config.yaml` — control matrix
- `.aof/adoption.yaml` — scoped adoption principles and skills
- `aof/conformance/gaps.md` — Deferred/Unsupported controls and warnings
- `aof/conformance/scope.yaml` — explicit scoped-conformance posture

`Deferred != Satisfied`, `Unsupported != Satisfied`, and `NotApplicable` MUST reflect true non-applicability rather than convenience.

## Operational Guidance

AI coding agents SHOULD use `AGENTS.md` as a router and load only relevant AOF skills. Rich project-specific context is kept under `aof/`; canonical static semantics remain grounded in AOF v1.0 LTS.
